  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nPR1611 certifies helper450's scalar restoration using sparse rational row/column propagation. This independently corroborates that scalar premise by pushing every input basis vector forward with a separately written exact dyadic implementation. No discrepancy was found. Only `research/k8-hpe450-forward-audit/` is added: eight files, including the checker, deterministic receipt, source pins and review/validation records.\n\nBoth pinned local orientations have 24,767 events and 19,693 scalar operations. All 1,424 basis executions confirm the unit helper output row, its isolated dirt column and zero coefficients from all eight arbitrary private inputs. Six malformed programs reject with explicit exact coefficient witnesses. A dirt-leaking read preserves the row but leaks 1/2 to L230 forward and 1 to L27 backward. This is finite corroboration, not a new identity, Lean theorem, supplier admission or kappa.\n\nThe retained conditional C7 conclusion still needs exact event recipes and JSON-to-Lean correspondence. COPY/CLEAR lifetimes, other recipes, hosting/footprints, all-size compilation, precision/tape, complete costs and analytic transfer remain open. Selected sources/frontier and predecessor packages are unchanged.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nBase current main `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`; contribution `a2078691245ff8d2825def7048680759b695cb49`. Task `formal-interface-lemma`, scope key `e3ffea67887eeb4c396c`, nonce `9c92a140d6ff014ccc0bdd30a86e9981`, revision 3. Scope refined to the scalar premise of one existing theorem-to-emission binding; exact card and stop rule are in TASK.json. [Claim](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1394#discussioncomment-18918131).\n\n- [PR1611](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1611), exact head `156cc788b5a8122b19686f015e5654b117e4389d`: construction/binding predecessor; the new algorithm obtains the row by forward basis execution rather than reverse covector propagation. Its published verifier separately passes all 28 controls. No pending checker code is imported.\n- [PR1415](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1415), `0d8d2c3a96346756f02563b401a042ab97198e20`: retained complex operator semantics, not repeated.\n- [PR1697](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1697): parallel all-511 cold-hyperplane operator binding, a distinct domain.\n\nFinal overlap at 07:25 UTC read 393 open PR bodies, including drafts, through an empty numbered page; the helper also searched 875 local records. Discussions1163/1166/1394 and the active board were read live. Full Discussion pagination was unavailable, the helper warns about its absent Discussion cache, and concurrent merges make numbered pagination non-atomic. No-match output is not a novelty certificate.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/k8-hpe450-forward-audit\n```\n\nRegistered replay passes on CPython3.12.14/macOS in 5.72s. Also passed: metadata/source pins, unchanged selected-record check, 18 repository onboarding tests, a read-only optimized source export without Git, source-drift and receipt-corruption rejection, and occupied-output preservation. Exact arithmetic is compared with Fraction over 4,624 operand pairs; a four-input dirty echo checks destructive COPY/CLEAR and inverse scales. Two bounded agent static reviews found no actionable issue. VALIDATION.json records actual commands/environment and separates negative exit codes from success.\n\nNo fresh Lean/Mathlib build, general serialization proof, physical hosting replay, full selected cold replay, hosted CI success or independent human review is claimed.\n\n## Credit\n\nHanson Sun/@bbMisk (PR1611); Jeremy Kothe (HPE/k8); DreamingOfClouds (wrappers/Lemmas A/G); icekylinx (compiler); Rohan Arun (packing); Josie Elliston and Sagar Thakrar (word/audit lineage); @commdata2338 (PR1415); Aaron Wang/navinor (distinct cold audit); Chafik Boukhalfa, Zhihao Chen and all retained realization contributors. New work by @ToikY with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in research, implementation, verification and writing, including bounded subagents. Apache-2.0; original notices unchanged.\n\n## Open next questions\n\n[README](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/a2078691245ff8d2825def7048680759b695cb49/research/k8-hpe450-forward-audit/README.md#open-next-questions) records the smallest useful follow-ups: translate this one helper into an actual Lean event word with private COPY/CLEAR lifetimes, or trace it through actual T16 hosted invocations. Scalar agreement does not discharge either missing correspondence or physical footprint proof.",
